{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"D (they/them)","id":"692746345387130900","is_bot":0,"username":"nonbianarydarry"},"author_id":"692746345387130900","channel_id":"852737863170654259","content":"\"another old story, love it! Faralei, what story will you tell us?\"","created_at":"2021-07-23T02:45:09.174000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"867960500200292382","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"chinea","id":"740639937677754539","is_bot":0,"username":"franczine"},"author_id":"740639937677754539","channel_id":"852737863170654259","content":"Faralei walks on to the stage, and starts to tell her story. Her voice is soft, as it echoes down the microphone.\n\n“This one time I saw a bug carrying a piece of bread that was like ***five times its size*** and he was carrying it *up stairs*. Like up and then he would turn and then it would go up and then he would turn.” \n\nShe imitates the motion of going up and down the stairs with her fingers. \n\nShe gives a satisfied sigh at recalling the memory. “Will wonders ever cease? But in the end, a bird flew in and picked up the bread. I assume the ant along with it.” She waves her hand, dismissively. As if the story’s turn was expected. She takes a deep breathe before continuing, and she switches the weight of her body to her right leg.\n\n“So… you know. The moral if the story is, ***death is inevitable***.” She takes a momentary pause to let the words sink in. “But what counts is how far you go, and how far you’re willing to push yourself before the end comes. **The. End.** “","created_at":"2021-07-23T02:45:20.938000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"867960549542068274","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
